<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kunersdorf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1759">1759</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kunersdorf was fought on 12 August 1759 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> an der Oder in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. A Russian army under Pyotr Saltykov and an Austrian corps under Ernst Gideon von Laudon crushed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>'s Prussian army, which lost about half its men. Frederick briefly despaired, but the allies failed to follow up their victory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kunersdorf.jpg" alt="Battle of Kunersdorf" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander von Kotzebue · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_von_Kotzebue_-_Battle_of_Kunersdorf_on_1_August_1759.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
